00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:08.250
ANUJ GOYAL: I'm Anuj Goyal.

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:13.790
I'm a product manager for
Chrome Browser Enterprise.

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:15.980
And here's the agenda today.

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:18.110
We're going to talk
about why the browser is

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:21.320
becoming increasingly
important in the enterprise.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:25.000
We're going to talk about
Chrome browser benefits,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.030
improvements since last year,
future enhancements that

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:33.440
are coming in 2019,
and finally, how to get

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:36.920
started managing Chrome
Browser Enterprise.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:40.240
So let's get started.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:45.250
We all know the way that
enterprise's work is changing.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:48.460
This is being driven by
rapid technology changes.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:52.060
What was once impossible
is now possible,

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:55.390
and what was once
possible is now normal.

00:00:55.390 --> 00:01:01.240
Employees want flexibility,
agility, speed, and access

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:04.209
to what they want
when they want it.

00:01:04.209 --> 00:01:06.670
People want to be able
to pick up their kids,

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:11.230
take calls from the car, work
from home, and respond to email

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:12.730
wherever they are.

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:16.480
We all know this and
experience this every day.

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:18.880
With the affordability
of cloud computing,

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.880
the reach of mobile
devices, and the ubiquity

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:26.470
of fast connectivity, technology
in the work environment

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:29.540
is vastly different
from what it used to be.

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:31.430
So let's look at some stats.

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:36.010
84% of people work in
virtual environments at least

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:37.840
part of the time.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:40.870
On average, an
employee has 22 apps

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:43.240
and they have three devices.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:45.460
Almost half of
those devices store

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:47.990
some business critical data.

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:53.110
And finally, remote work
is the norm for about 70%

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:55.105
of your traditional
information workers.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:02.170
So what you need
is a secure browser

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:04.960
that can be managed
centrally while keeping

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:07.180
employees productive.

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.340
Big drum roll.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:11.470
That's Chrome
Browser Enterprise.

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:15.940
It provides secure, trusted
access to data, apps, and cloud

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:17.770
services.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:21.550
The browser also connects
employees on any device

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:25.480
and proactively protects
users while they work.

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:29.470
Your users get a consistent,
customizable experience

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:32.830
wherever they want to
work, and IT admins

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:36.280
can easily manage
permissions and policies

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:40.600
across every user, every
device, and every platform

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:43.450
that they have in
their enterprise.

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:47.770
It should be no surprise to
learn that Chrome browser has

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:50.680
been evolving over
the past 10 years

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:53.770
to support enterprise users.

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:57.010
We started with
administrative GPOs

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.470
and then we added features,
additional features,

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:03.850
that customers requested
for enterprise use cases.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:09.310
As the web has grown, so have
our enterprise capabilities.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:11.620
Also in the past year,
we've added the ability

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:15.640
to manage Chrome browser
from Google's Admin Console.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:18.880
And we'll detail additional
feature enhancements

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:22.050
later in the presentation.

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:23.790
First, let's talk
about the impact

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:26.700
that Chrome can have on
an average enterprise

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:29.460
of about 20,000 employees.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:33.570
Forrester Consulting
has said, one, Chrome

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:38.700
is easier to troubleshoot, and
two, help desk turnaround times

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:40.900
are much, much faster.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:44.490
So overall, end user
productivity increases

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:50.400
and enterprises see tangible
benefits within six months.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.980
This further validates that
Chrome browser can enable

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:57.150
your IT admins, IT help
desk, and employees

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:59.170
to be more productive.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:01.660
So quick poll of the audience.

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:05.610
How many of you are Chrome
Browser Enterprise users?

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:06.270
Hands higher.

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:06.820
Come on.

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:07.320
Come on.

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:07.860
Thank you.

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:10.390
I appreciate it.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:14.880
All right, let's talk about
what we've done since last year.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:19.829
First, we've improved security
in many, many different ways.

00:04:19.829 --> 00:04:22.079
The web is a dangerous
place, and we

00:04:22.079 --> 00:04:24.810
have blocked third
party processes

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:27.150
from hijacking Chrome.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:30.570
Two, we've improved the
verification process

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:35.100
for extensions, and we've
prevented deceptive extensions

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:38.730
from being installed
in the enterprise.

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:43.110
Three, we've let enterprise
users know if their enterprise

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:46.800
password has been
compromised and if it's being

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:49.540
used outside of their company.

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:53.700
And last, we've rolled out site
isolation to contain threats.

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:56.520
This is a key differentiator
of Chrome browser

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:57.975
to keep your end users safe.

00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:04.570
But, but, but, but no
security discussion

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:07.420
would be complete
without discussing Flash.

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:08.890
For the past 20 years--

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:10.780
yeah, you can laugh.

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:12.730
For the past 20 years,
Flash has helped

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:16.180
shape the way that you
play games, browse the web,

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:19.240
watch videos, and
run applications.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:21.190
But over the last
few years, Flash

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:23.740
has actually become less common.

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:28.870
Three years ago,
80% of Flash users--

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:32.620
excuse me, 80% of Chrome
users visited a Flash website

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.630
once a day.

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:40.750
Now Flash usage is only 6%,
and it continues to decline.

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:42.520
This trend shows
that websites are

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:48.070
moving to open web technologies
such as HTML5 and PWAs,

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:52.120
which are faster and more
efficient than Flash.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:55.300
So IT admins, hopefully
I'm looking at all of you,

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:57.520
please work with
your software vendors

00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:00.625
to find a migration
path away from Flash.

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:06.930
Since Next 2013,
we've also streamlined

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:10.150
how are browsers managed
in existing environments.

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:12.130
For example, we
know a lot of you

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:16.570
use third party tools
such as SCCM and Intune

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:18.950
to manage your applications.

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:22.840
We verified that Chrome browser
GPOs can be configured properly

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:26.110
from these tools and
improved our documentation

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:31.280
to help admins configure
Chrome within these tools.

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:34.760
We've tested that browser
sign in and restrict

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:37.970
sign in pattern
policies work together

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:41.870
to ensure that your users
can sign into Chrome browser

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:44.870
with the correct work email.

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:48.200
Third, many customers
want statistics on how

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:51.380
their users use Chrome browser.

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:54.920
We've built a purely
optional extension

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:59.180
that an administrator can
install on a Chrome browser.

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:02.450
They can monitor the resource
consumption of Chrome browser

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:06.510
by memory, they can see
they're signed in status,

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:08.930
they can see the
connectivity of the device,

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:13.040
and many, many other
machine information--

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:16.490
excuse me, machine
configuration policies.

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:21.450
The extension data is stored
locally in JSON on that device.

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:25.430
So you can use Splunk or
SCCM to read that information

00:07:25.430 --> 00:07:28.300
and build your own reports.

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:32.310
Fourth, we've added
relaunch notifications.

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:35.690
These policies allow
you to influence

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:38.000
how often your
user gets reminded

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:41.690
that a new version of Chrome
is available to download.

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:43.250
And many of our
customers had said

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:46.700
that this helps quite a bit with
keeping their users on the most

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:47.960
current version of Chrome.

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:53.400
This is another feature that
we've added recently called

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:56.640
managed by, and it was
built with a lot of feedback

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:59.230
from your employees.

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:00.900
It helps increase
the transparency

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:03.900
between admins and end users.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:08.040
We're letting employees easily
see the administrative policies

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:10.770
that are being set up
in their environment

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:14.490
so that they know their
browser is being managed.

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:17.950
We definitely expect some
discussion around this feature,

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:21.443
so we will continue to iterate
on it over the next few months

00:08:21.443 --> 00:08:22.235
with your feedback.

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:31.180
Now let's move on to
what's happening in 2019.

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:34.299
This is our forward
looking roadmap.

00:08:34.299 --> 00:08:36.789
We have a lot of
great features coming.

00:08:36.789 --> 00:08:40.105
And I'm going to discuss each
one of these in more detail.

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:47.590
So first, Chrome Browser cloud
management has just launched.

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:50.020
This will enable
admins to easily manage

00:08:50.020 --> 00:08:53.980
Chrome deployments of
any size from the cloud.

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:57.670
Admins can enroll devices
into organizational units

00:08:57.670 --> 00:09:00.880
and manage all the
desktop Chrome browsers

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:04.900
of these enrolled devices
through Google Admin Console.

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:08.740
They can also apply policies
to organizational units

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:14.350
and deploy those policies to all
the browsers that are enrolled.

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:18.100
Admins will be able to gain
insights into their deployment,

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:19.810
and they will be
able to delegate

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:21.680
admin responsibilities.

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:23.950
So if you have a
large organization,

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:28.150
you could delegate an admin
for finance, an admin for HR,

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:31.390
an admin for sales, an
admin for any other group

00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:34.510
that you might have
in your organization.

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:39.250
Note that administrators need
to have a Google account,

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:42.220
but your end users do not.

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:45.550
What we do is that
we enroll the browser

00:09:45.550 --> 00:09:49.960
via a token, which admins can
retrieve from the Google Admin

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:51.580
Console.

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:54.010
There's a lot of great
features in this product,

00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:57.070
and I won't be able to cover
them all in this session.

00:09:57.070 --> 00:10:00.040
Please check out the session
later today with my colleague

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:03.190
Phil and Starbucks
to learn how they

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:05.230
have deployed
Chrome Browser cloud

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:06.710
management at their company.

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:13.198
Next feature, legacy
browser support.

00:10:13.198 --> 00:10:14.740
This is a feature
that we've actually

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:18.400
had for a couple years that
allows admins to have Chrome

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:22.600
as the default browser for the
majority of their websites,

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:25.990
but it will allow them to
automatically fall back

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:28.570
to a legacy browser
for some minority

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:31.450
set of legacy websites.

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:35.110
In addition, users are endlessly
switched back to Chrome

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:36.790
from that legacy
browser when they

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:39.130
try to access a modern website.

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:42.040
So it's really, really useful.

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:44.590
While this feature has been
available for many years,

00:10:44.590 --> 00:10:47.140
it's now going to be
much easier to deploy,

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:49.480
because it's being
built into Chrome

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:53.720
and you won't have to rely
on an additional extension.

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:55.600
We've actually heard a
lot of great feedback

00:10:55.600 --> 00:10:59.950
from this feature from early
adopters of the integrated LBS,

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:01.480
and we really hope
to hear from you

00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:04.940
and hope that you
enjoy it as well.

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:07.820
We will also be adding
controls for legacy browser

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:11.320
support into the Admin
Console later this year.

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:18.670
Another feature that
is getting rolled out

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:22.510
is part of a suite of features
called Update Controls.

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:25.030
Many of our customers
have requested the ability

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:28.540
to pin Chrome to
specific versions.

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:30.460
We launched this
feature, and it's

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:32.160
really meant for
companies-- excuse me,

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:33.660
we've already
launched this feature,

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:35.920
and we've gotten
feedback from companies,

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:38.560
and they've told us this is
super helpful when they have

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:43.390
strict management, change
management requirements

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:46.750
and or compliance needs.

00:11:46.750 --> 00:11:50.320
What we are now doing is
offering a way for customers

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:53.260
to roll back a new
version of Chrome

00:11:53.260 --> 00:11:56.170
to an old version of Chrome.

00:11:56.170 --> 00:11:59.800
And this is meant as a
temporary measure or emergency

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:01.240
workaround.

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:04.480
We always recommend to stay on
the newest version of Chrome

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:09.130
so that you're up to date with
the latest security patches.

00:12:09.130 --> 00:12:12.610
Today these features are
available as GPO only,

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:15.250
and we will add these
controls to the Admin Console

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:16.060
later this year.

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:20.730
Next, how many of
you use passwords?

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:21.750
I use passwords.

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:24.240
I have a corporate password.

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:27.090
Sometimes I accidentally
use that password outside

00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:28.780
of my company.

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:32.580
So we've built a feature
called Password Alert.

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:34.800
This will alert
your employees when

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:37.080
they use their
corporate password

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:40.050
on a non-whitelisted website.

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:42.330
And what the feature
does, it will actually

00:12:42.330 --> 00:12:45.870
instruct them to
reset their password.

00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:47.910
This prevents
corporate passwords

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:53.760
from being phished by
malicious, third party websites.

00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:57.390
We also plan to enable Password
Alert from the Admin Console

00:12:57.390 --> 00:13:00.060
so that IT admins
can get reports

00:13:00.060 --> 00:13:03.990
on who is reusing their password
outside of their company.

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:06.450
This helps quite a
bit for compliance.

00:13:10.450 --> 00:13:10.950
Next.

00:13:13.950 --> 00:13:18.130
Chrome browser has
a ton of policies.

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:20.340
We know that we've had
to make improvements

00:13:20.340 --> 00:13:22.980
towards documenting
these policies,

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:26.010
and we're going to
update our policy page.

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:28.740
Right now when you go
to our policy list,

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:33.600
it's a huge, just
gigantic web page of 300

00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:38.700
plus policies that span
Chrome Browser and Chrome OS.

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:41.130
You've asked for an
easier way to search

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:44.220
through these policies, and
that's what we're doing.

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:47.190
You're going to be able to
filter by operating system,

00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:49.830
you're going to be able to
filter by browser version,

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:54.660
and you're going to be able to
filter by a couple other things

00:13:54.660 --> 00:13:59.370
to more easily allow you to see
when a new policy was added.

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:05.540
Onto Omnibox.

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:08.250
Omnibox is one of my
most favorite features,

00:14:08.250 --> 00:14:12.840
and we continue to look at
Omnibox as a key entry point

00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:15.790
for surfacing search results.

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:18.630
Now G Suite admins
have the option

00:14:18.630 --> 00:14:21.870
to allow Chrome Omnibox
to show document

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:26.460
suggestions from Google Drive
when a user does a search.

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:30.100
And this is all enabled from
within your company firewall,

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:32.730
not external.

00:14:32.730 --> 00:14:35.310
Note that there are three
things that an admin must

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:37.620
do to enable this feature.

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:40.050
One, you have to have
a G Suite account,

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:42.630
and you have to turn
on this setting.

00:14:42.630 --> 00:14:47.550
Two, users have to be
signed into Chrome.

00:14:47.550 --> 00:14:49.170
That should be obvious.

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:54.240
And three, users have to
have Cloud Sync turned on.

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:56.220
We use this feature
every day Google,

00:14:56.220 --> 00:14:58.650
and I can tell you it's
super useful for finding

00:14:58.650 --> 00:15:00.495
that document that you
just can't remember.

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:07.700
Another UX related
feature is tab groups,

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:09.370
which is super amazing.

00:15:09.370 --> 00:15:11.650
Tab groups will increase
the productivity

00:15:11.650 --> 00:15:13.960
for users that want
better tools to manage

00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:17.590
their workflows, especially
their business workflows.

00:15:17.590 --> 00:15:19.660
You'll be able to
group related tabs

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:22.780
together so that it's easier
to find your work stream

00:15:22.780 --> 00:15:23.500
and stay focused.

00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:29.870
And those are some
of our major features

00:15:29.870 --> 00:15:32.870
that are coming in 2019.

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:35.330
Just as a reminder, we
have an extensive list

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:39.950
of resources for our customers
that don't buy support.

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:43.640
We have release notes,
help center articles,

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:46.350
and a free enterprise forum.

00:15:46.350 --> 00:15:49.400
And if you're interested
in purchasing support,

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:53.270
please contact our Chrome
enterprise browser specialists

00:15:53.270 --> 00:15:55.850
at google.com and
they'll tell you

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:59.030
what's included in
the support package.

00:15:59.030 --> 00:16:00.620
Noriko is right back there.

00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:01.832
She's smiling.

00:16:01.832 --> 00:16:03.290
Go say hi to her
after the session.

00:16:06.948 --> 00:16:08.890
All right.

00:16:08.890 --> 00:16:12.340
We're almost done, but we
have many other sessions

00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:16.360
